# What must never reach the build context.
#
# Two jobs. The first is security: an .env or a credentials directory copied into
# a layer stays in the image forever, even if a later layer deletes it. The
# second is speed: the build context is uploaded to the daemon before anything
# runs, and the corpus plus git history is most of this repository's bytes.
#
# NOTE the deliberate omission: vendor/ is NOT ignored. The image is built with
# -mod=vendor precisely so the build needs no network (see Dockerfile).

# Secrets — same list as .gitignore, restated because .dockerignore does not
# inherit it and a mistake here is worse.
.env
.env.*
*.local
credentials/
deploy/*.env
!deploy/env.example

# VCS and CI
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Build outputs and caches
bin/
dist/
coverage.out
*.exe

# Test fixtures and spike material: several megabytes that no production build
# reads. The MIME corpus is a test asset (S4), exercised by `go test`, never by
# the binary.
testdata/
spikes/
docs/
patches/

# Node
node_modules/

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
